    "background_story": "Irene was a brilliant mathematician with a passion for geometry. Growing up, she spent hours poring over her father's old textbooks, fascinated by the intricate relationships between lines and curves. Her fascination with the secant line, which intersects a circle at two points, led her to develop a groundbreaking new theorem. The 'Irene's Secant Theorem' revolutionized the field of mathematics, providing a novel approach to solving complex geometric problems. As news of her discovery spread, Irene became an overnight sensation in the academic community, hailed as a rising star in the world of mathematics. Her work inspired a new generation of mathematicians and scientists, and her name became synonymous with innovation and intellectual curiosity.",
